Example of primary_stack against a posting that states its stack twice:
Input: must-have qualifications say "Proficiency in Java and/or Python"; a
later "Core Technical Stack" section lists "Java and Python, Apache Kafka, GCP
(BigQuery, GKE, Vertex AI), Snowflake and Starburst/Trino, Terraform, Scrapy,
proxy management systems, Apache Airflow".
-> primary_stack is ["Java | Python", "Apache Kafka", "GCP", "Kubernetes"]
The language requirement stays ONE entry because the must-have section offers
the two as substitutes, and the bare "Java and Python" in the stack listing does
not override that — the stricter statement governs. Snowflake, Terraform,
Scrapy, and Airflow remain in required_skills but are not what the role is built
on. Note this is independent of required_skills, which still lists every one of
them separately.
